      "Frame 5: robot_1 makes another small adjustment toward the bin, moving its body slightly rightward while keeping the gripper arm folded above its back. Its feet occupy a narrower area in front of trash_bin_1 than in the initial frame. The bin's lid remains down, and packaging_1 is still on floor_1 beside the bin's right edge, close to the robot's bin-facing end. refrigerator_1 and its freezer door remain closed, as does oven_1. cooktop_1, pot_1, range_hood_1, and upper_cabinet_1 remain unchanged. countertop_1, sink_1, faucet_1, and window_1 retain their positions. lower_cabinet_1, drawer_unit_1, lower_cabinet_2, drawer_unit_2, and lower_cabinet_3 remain closed. container_1, container_2, container_3, container_4, and countertop_items_1 are stationary. backsplash_1 and floor_1 show no change. The refrigerator and oven remain separated from the robot by substantially more space than the bin.",
      "Frame 6: robot_1 completes its approach and stands almost directly in front of trash_bin_1, with its body less than one body length from the cabinet fronts. Its arm is still held roughly horizontally, extending across the bin area above the torso. The four feet are spread for support, with little remaining body translation. trash_bin_1 remains closed; packaging_1 is visible just to its right near the robot's forward-right side. refrigerator_1 and oven_1 remain closed. cooktop_1 and pot_1 are unchanged beneath range_hood_1 and upper_cabinet_1. countertop_1, sink_1, faucet_1, and window_1 remain stationary. lower_cabinet_1, drawer_unit_1, lower_cabinet_2, drawer_unit_2, and lower_cabinet_3 are closed. container_1, container_2, and container_3 remain near the cooktop; container_4 and countertop_items_1 remain near the sink. backsplash_1 and floor_1 are unchanged.",
      "Frame 7: robot_1 holds approximately the same body position while rotating and folding its arm. The previously horizontal yellow arm segment swings into a more diagonal, compact configuration above the bin-facing end of the torso, and the gripper is repositioned toward the area beside trash_bin_1. The bin remains closed. packaging_1 is still discernible near the bin's right base, although the robot increasingly overlaps that area. refrigerator_1 and oven_1 remain closed; cooktop_1, pot_1, range_hood_1, and upper_cabinet_1 are stationary. countertop_1, sink_1, faucet_1, and window_1 remain unchanged. lower_cabinet_1, drawer_unit_1, lower_cabinet_2, drawer_unit_2, and lower_cabinet_3 remain closed. container_1, container_2, container_3, container_4, and countertop_items_1 retain their positions. backsplash_1 and floor_1 are unchanged. Arm motion, rather than walking, is now the principal visible movement.",
