      "Frame 12: Robot_arm_1 lowers the held large bowl toward the left edge of table_1. Its lower surface is closer to tabletop height than in the preceding frame, while the gripper remains firmly positioned on the right rim. Bowl_3 stays upright to the lower right; the nearest bowl edges remain visibly separated. Bowl_2 remains obscured or visually merged with other bowl surfaces. The held bowl's empty, reflective interior faces upward and toward the camera. The arm occupies the upper-left region. Crate_1, cabinet_1, laptop_1, and stand_1 remain behind it, bin_1 remains partially visible at the lower left, and stand_2 remains on the gray floor at the upper right.",
      "Frame 13: The large bowl shifts slightly upward while remaining near the left border. Robot_arm_1's gripper maintains the same right-rim contact, and the wrist stays nearly vertical. The bowl is suspended beside table_1 rather than placed on it. Bowl_3 has not changed position or orientation and remains diagonally below-right, with a clear gap from the held bowl. Bowl_2 cannot be independently identified in this image. Reflections change slightly across the metal interiors as the robot moves. Crate_1, cabinet_1, laptop_1, stand_1, bin_1, and stand_2 remain stationary, with the worn tabletop and its central black patches otherwise unobstructed.",
      "Frame 14: Robot_arm_1 holds the large bowl slightly higher, with only a small change in lateral position. Its rim is near the left image edge, and its right side remains in the gripper. The bowl's upward-facing interior is clearly visible. Bowl_3 remains still on table_1 below-right, and there is no visible contact between the two exposed bowls. Bowl_2 remains hidden from independent inspection. The arm's pale-blue joint and silver wrist occupy the upper part of the frame, while the gripper is close to the bowl but not close to bowl_3. Crate_1, cabinet_1 with laptop_1, stand_1, bin_1, and stand_2 remain unchanged.",
