      "Frame 16: Robot_arm_1 raises the large bowl a small amount and shifts it slightly right. The gripper-to-rim relationship is unchanged, and the bowl continues to face upward toward the camera. Bowl_3 remains upright and motionless on table_1, separated from the held bowl by a visible strip of background or tabletop. Bowl_2 remains unresolvable as a separate object. The wrist is positioned above the space left of bowl_3 rather than over its center. The blue crate_1, white cabinet_1, laptop_1 on the cabinet, black stand_1, partially visible bin_1, and distant stand_2 all remain in their original positions.",
      "Frame 17: The robot moves the held large bowl noticeably rightward, bringing it farther over the back-left corner of table_1. Its lower-right side is now closer to bowl_3's upper-left rim, though the bowls remain separated and at different heights. Robot_arm_1 keeps its gripper on the large bowl's right rim and its wrist vertical. Bowl_3 does not move, and bowl_2 remains concealed or not independently distinguishable. The large bowl's reflective interior and outer wall are both visible. Crate_1, cabinet_1 with laptop_1, and stand_1 remain behind the robot; bin_1 stays cropped at the lower left, and stand_2 remains on the upper-right floor.",
      "Frame 18: The large bowl moves back left, nearly touching the image boundary with its rim. Robot_arm_1 remains connected at the bowl's right edge, holding it above the side of table_1. This leftward shift increases its lateral separation from bowl_3, which stays upright at the same foreground position. Bowl_2 is still not visible as a separate bowl. The wrist and pale-blue joint remain overhead, with no visible contact between the robot and the small bowl. The wooden surface and dark patches remain unchanged. Crate_1, cabinet_1, laptop_1, stand_1, bin_1, and stand_2 remain stationary around the table.",
      "Frame 19: Robot_arm_1 lifts the large bowl higher at the far left. The bowl's bottom rises well above the tabletop, and its opening remains angled upward toward the camera. The gripper continues to pinch or hold the right rim. Bowl_3 remains unmoved on table_1, clearly lower and to the right of the raised bowl. Bowl_2 is not independently visible. The robot's higher position exposes more of the left edge of the worktable beneath the bowl. Crate_1, cabinet_1, laptop_1, and stand_1 retain their background arrangement; bin_1 remains partly visible in the lower-left corner, and stand_2 remains fixed at the upper right.",
      "Frame 20: The held large bowl moves down and right, returning above the back-left portion of table_1. Robot_arm_1's gripper stays at its right rim, with the vertical wrist directly above that contact. The bowl approaches the region just above-left of bowl_3, but a visible gap remains between their rims. Bowl_3 continues to rest upright without displacement. Bowl_2 remains hidden or indistinguishable within the visible metal surfaces. The table's central and right sections remain empty. Crate_1, cabinet_1 with laptop_1, stand_1, the cropped bin_1, and stand_2 show no change in position.",
      "Frame 21: Robot_arm_1 raises the large bowl sharply relative to the preceding frame, keeping it left of bowl_3. The bowl's lower edge is now substantially above the wood, increasing the vertical gap from the small bowl. Its opening remains upward-facing, and the gripper is still attached at the right rim. Bowl_3 remains stationary on table_1, and bowl_2 is not separately visible. The held bowl partly overlaps the white cabinet in the background. Crate_1 remains to the cabinet's left, laptop_1 stays on top, stand_1 remains around the equipment, bin_1 remains cropped at the lower left, and stand_2 stays at the upper right.",
      "Frame 22: The large bowl is lowered again near the left side of table_1, reversing the preceding upward movement. Robot_arm_1 maintains its right-rim grip, with the bowl's bottom closer to tabletop height and its interior still visible. Bowl_3 remains upright and still to the lower right; there is no visible rim contact between the bowls. Bowl_2 remains unresolved as a separate object. The pale-blue joint and gray links occupy the upper-left corner. Crate_1, cabinet_1, laptop_1, stand_1, the partially cropped gray bin_1, and stand_2 remain stationary, and the table's dark central marks stay exposed.",
      "Frame 23: More of robot_arm_1's bent gray links and pale-blue joint enters from the top as the wrist and large bowl move lower and left. The bowl is suspended beside the left-front region of table_1, with its right rim held by the gripper. Bowl_3 remains in its original position to the right, with the held bowl's lower-right edge approaching its left side but not visibly touching it. Bowl_2 is not independently visible. The low bowl partly overlaps the area above bin_1. Crate_1, cabinet_1 with laptop_1, stand_1, and stand_2 remain fixed in the background.",
