      "Frame 1: The wooden worktable fills most of the view, with scratches and colored marks surrounding a flat pink drawstring bag near its center. The bag's white graphic faces upward, and its cream cords form loose loops beyond its upper corners. The Labubu plush toy is not visible. The left/rear robotic arm holds its open angular gripper above and behind the bag, several gripper-widths away; the right/foreground arm and open gripper are farther right and partially cropped. Both arms are clear of the tabletop objects. The computer tower and its illuminated fan sit behind the arms, beside the bolted black metal mounting frame. Electrical cables drape along the arm links and rear equipment.",
      "Frame 2: The pink bag remains flat on the scratched wooden worktable in essentially the same position and orientation, with the white graphic upward and the drawstring loops loosely extended. No plush toy is visible. Both robotic arms remain raised and separated from the bag: the left/rear gripper is above its far side, and the right/foreground gripper is near the right edge. Neither gripper contacts the fabric or cords. The computer tower's circular fan is now visibly blue-lit. The black mounting frame remains fixed at the table's right edge, and the electrical cable bundle retains its loose routing around the apparatus.",
      "Frame 3: Both robotic arms have swung inward over the wooden worktable. The left/rear gripper points downward above the bag's far edge, while the larger foreground wrist and right gripper move into the upper-right central view. The fingertips remain visibly above the bag, with a gap on the order of one or two gripper lengths in projection. The pink bag is still flat, and its drawstrings remain spread on the wood; the Labubu toy is not visible. The arms partly obscure the computer tower and black mounting frame. Attached electrical cables bend into broader hanging curves as the wrists move.",
      "Frame 4: The left/rear gripper has descended to the bag's drawstring edge, with its tips immediately beside or against the gathered pink fabric. The right/foreground gripper is close to the same area from the right, and the two wrists overlap visually. The pink bag has shifted toward the camera and rotated slightly, with its lower end now closer to the bottom edge; its right cord trails in a loose curve across the wooden surface. No plush toy is visible. The computer tower and mounting frame remain stationary behind the arms, while the electrical cables flex around the lowered joints.",
      "Frame 5: Both grippers remain tightly clustered over the upper edge of the pink bag. The left/rear fingertips meet the gathered drawstring region, while the right/foreground gripper sits immediately beside it, partly concealing the contact area. The bag is elongated toward the bottom of the wooden worktable view, with new folds near its upper edge and the white graphic still facing upward. Cream cords lie on either side of the grippers. The Labubu toy remains out of sight. The computer tower and black mounting frame are unchanged, and the electrical cables hang around the closely spaced wrists without visible contact with the bag.",
      "Frame 6: The left/rear gripper is centered directly over the bag's gathered opening, with its tips at the fabric edge. The right/foreground gripper has moved slightly upward and right, leaving a small visible gap from the bag. The pink bag has slid leftward and lies flatter on the wooden surface, with its white graphic near the upper half and cords stretching out to both sides. No Labubu toy is exposed. The computer tower and bolted mounting frame remain in the background. The arm wiring follows the repositioned joints, including a loop hanging beneath the foreground wrist.",
      "Frame 7: The left/rear gripper presses down at the pink bag's upper seam or cord channel, its tips touching the gathered edge. The right/foreground gripper hovers close by, roughly a gripper-width to the right of that contact. The bag extends toward and partly beyond the lower image boundary, with the white silhouette still upward and cream drawstrings resting across the scratched wood. The Labubu toy is not visible. The computer tower and black mounting frame stay fixed behind the arms, and the electrical cable bundle bends around the low wrists.",
      "Frame 8: A narrow gap is now visible between the left/rear gripper tips and the bag's gathered top edge as that gripper rises slightly. The right/foreground gripper remains suspended nearby to the right, also clear of the fabric. The pink bag stays flat and elongated toward the camera, with its upper corners puckered and both cords spread on the worktable. No plush toy is visible. The computer tower, mounting frame, and tabletop remain stationary. Electrical leads curve beneath the arm links, changing slightly with the raised left wrist.",
      "Frame 9: The right/foreground arm swings down and left across the view, bringing its gripper over the middle-to-upper portion of the pink bag and partially blocking the white graphic. The left/rear gripper remains near the drawstring edge behind it. The right fingertips reach the fabric surface, while the bag remains largely supported by the wooden table. The cream cords are visible around the bag's far edge; no Labubu toy is exposed. The computer tower and mounting frame are increasingly occluded by the foreground arm. The attached cables sweep with the wrist and form a broad loop to its right.",
      "Frame 10: The right/foreground gripper is closed against a raised fold of pink fabric near the bag's upper portion. The left/rear gripper remains just behind it near the opposite edge. The bag is lifting from its flat position: its upper section rises between the grippers while its lower portion still touches the scratched wooden worktable. Much of the printed surface is hidden by the wrists and folds. The Labubu toy is not yet visible. The stationary computer tower and black mounting frame remain in the right background, with electrical cables bowing around the elevated fabric and arm joints.",
      "Frame 11: The pink bag is now held nearly upright beneath the two closely spaced grippers. Its lower corner remains very near or lightly against the wooden tabletop, while the upper rim is elevated. A pale inner section is visible at the mouth, but no distinct Labubu toy can yet be identified. The left/rear gripper holds near the upper-left side of the rim, and the right/foreground gripper is positioned at the upper-right side. A drawstring hangs in a loose arc to the left. The computer tower, black mounting frame, and routed cable bundle remain behind the arms.",
      "Frame 12: Both grippers remain close to the elevated mouth of the upright pink bag. The right/foreground wrist has rotated slightly, shifting its fingers along the rim while the left/rear gripper supports the nearby upper edge. The bag hangs downward with its lower tip near the wood, and its white printed silhouette remains visible on the front-facing panel. The opening shows pale fabric but no clearly distinguishable plush toy. The computer tower and black mounting frame stay fixed, while electrical cables bend around the wrists and trail back toward the equipment.",
      "Frame 13: The left/rear gripper continues holding the bag near its upper-left edge. The right/foreground gripper has rotated outward and opened wider beside the upper-right rim, making its two separated angular fingers more visible. The bag remains mostly upright, with its bottom grazing or nearly grazing the wooden worktable and its cream cords hanging leftward. No distinct Labubu toy is visible. The computer tower's illuminated fan is partly visible through the robot structure. The black mounting frame remains stationary, and the electrical cable loop shifts with the right wrist.",
      "Frame 14: The right/foreground gripper has repositioned against the bag's upper-right fabric while the left/rear gripper stays at the opposite upper edge. The bag twists slightly, revealing more pale material around its opening and changing the angle of the front printed panel. Its lower end stays close to the wooden surface. The Labubu toy is still not clearly exposed. The arms are nearly touching each other around the rim, with essentially no gap between their active fingertips and the fabric. The computer tower, mounting frame, and electrical wiring remain in their background locations.",
      "Frame 15: The two arms rotate the suspended pink bag so that it appears narrower and more edge-on to the camera. Both grippers are concentrated at its top, and the drawstrings bunch and dangle around their fingers. The bag's lower section hangs almost vertically, with its bottom close to the wooden worktable. No identifiable plush toy is visible outside the bag. The foreground arm obscures much of the computer tower, while portions of the black mounting frame remain visible at right. Electrical cables follow the changed wrist angles in curved hanging runs.",
      "Frame 16: The pink bag remains upright and narrow in profile, held near its top between the overlapping grippers. The right/foreground wrist has shifted slightly left and down, and the left/rear gripper remains immediately behind the gathered rim. The lower bag panel hangs toward the wood, with a cream cord loop visible against its side. The Labubu toy is not clearly visible. The wooden worktable and right-side mounting frame are stationary. The computer tower remains partly occluded, and the cable bundle flexes around the rotated wrists.",
      "Frame 17: The bag turns further, exposing more of its opposite pink panel and white decorative printing. The right/foreground gripper stays against the upper edge, while the left/rear gripper is close behind and slightly to the left. The bag hangs vertically with its base at or just above the tabletop, and the drawstrings remain gathered near the grippers. The Labubu plush is not yet separately visible. The computer tower and black metal mounting frame remain fixed behind the robot. Electrical cables curve across the upper-right portion of the scene and beneath the foreground wrist.",
      "Frame 18: The pink bag has been lowered onto the wooden worktable with its opposite printed side facing upward. It lies diagonally toward the bottom-right edge, and white lettering or decorative marks are visible but not reliably readable. The left/rear gripper is open and lifted just above the bag's upper-left area, while the right/foreground gripper remains low over its nearer panel. The Labubu toy is not exposed. The computer tower and black mounting frame are unchanged in the background. The cable bundle follows the spread between the two arms.",
      "Frame 19: Both arms descend over the flattened pink bag. The right/foreground gripper is very close to or pressing its nearer fabric panel, while the left/rear gripper approaches the drawstring opening from the upper-left side. The robot wrists obscure most of the bag, though pink fabric and a cream cord remain visible on the wooden tabletop. No distinct Labubu toy is visible. The computer tower remains behind the apparatus, partly blocked by the arms. The black mounting frame stays bolted in place, and electrical cables hang in arcs beside the low foreground wrist.",
      "Frame 20: The two grippers remain low over the bag, separated by only a small distance. The right/foreground fingers contact the near portion of the pink fabric, and the left/rear gripper is positioned at its farther edge. The bag is mostly hidden beneath the wrists, with its lower-right panel extending toward the image boundary. The Labubu toy cannot be distinguished. The scratched wooden table supports the fabric throughout. The computer tower, black mounting frame, and background cable routing remain stationary, while the arm-mounted leads bend around the closely folded joints.",
      "Frame 21: The right/foreground gripper maintains contact near the bag's lower visible panel, while the left/rear gripper remains at the far rim. There is little visible change in the bag's position: it stays flattened and partly concealed beneath the arms on the wooden worktable. A small section of cream drawstring is visible to the left of the wrists. No plush toy is clearly exposed. The computer tower and mounting frame remain fixed at the right rear. Electrical cables retain their hanging loops around the robot, with only slight changes in curvature.",
      "Frame 22: The left/rear arm swings inward and lower behind the foreground wrist, bringing its gripper closer to the bag's opening. The right/foreground gripper stays low against the near fabric, and their contact region becomes more heavily occluded. Pink material remains visible below the arms on the wooden tabletop, but the Labubu toy is not distinguishable. The bag's cords lie near its far-left edge. The computer tower and black mounting frame remain stationary in the background. The left arm's electrical leads bend more sharply as its elbow and wrist fold inward.",
      "Frame 23: The left/rear gripper has moved back slightly and is visible above the bag's far rim. The right/foreground gripper stays near the nearer portion, with the two arms now more separated. The pink bag's mouth is more visible as a rounded, raised opening, showing pale interior material while the lower panel remains on the wooden worktable. No clear plush face or body is yet visible. The computer tower and mounting frame are partly exposed between the arms. Electrical cables hang beside the foreground wrist and along the rear arm.",
      "Frame 24: The left/rear gripper lifts the bag's far edge, raising and opening the mouth while the right/foreground gripper remains down near the front panel. The bag forms a shallow upright cavity rather than lying completely flat, with pale lining visible inside and cream cords draped around its upper-left side. The Labubu toy is still not clearly distinguishable. The scratched wooden worktable supports the bag's base. The computer tower and bolted black mounting frame remain fixed, and the electrical cable bundle curves around the spread wrists without visibly contacting the opening.",
      "Frame 25: The left/rear gripper remains at the raised back rim of the pink bag, while the right/foreground wrist shifts slightly left over its front edge. The bag mouth stays open, with pale interior fabric visible between the arms, and the lower panel lies on the wooden worktable. No distinct toy features are visible through the partially blocked opening. Both grippers are at fabric-contact distance. The computer tower and mounting frame remain stationary behind the arms. Electrical wires move with the foreground wrist, maintaining a long loop along its right side.",
      "Frame 26: The right/foreground gripper moves across the near edge of the pink bag and remains close to the tabletop, while the left/rear gripper stays near the far opening. The bag is compressed and partly flattened beneath them, with pink folds and white interior material visible around the wrists. The Labubu toy is not yet clearly separated from the bag. The computer tower, mounting frame, and wood surface retain their positions. The arm-mounted electrical cables flex around the low, inward-facing grippers.",
      "Frame 27: The left/rear gripper rises above the bag with its fingers open. A gray-beige fuzzy object, now beginning to reveal the Labubu plush toy, is visible at the bag's upper-left opening on the wooden tabletop. The right/foreground gripper remains low over the pink bag's nearer section, keeping that panel beneath its fingers. The toy is only partly exposed and remains close to the bag. The computer tower and black mounting frame remain fixed at the right rear, while the left arm's electrical leads lift with its wrist.",
      "Frame 28: The left/rear gripper descends toward the exposed gray-beige plush at the bag's upper-left edge. Its fingers approach the toy's upper portion, reducing the gap to near contact. The right/foreground gripper stays against or immediately above the pink fabric nearer the camera. The Labubu toy is partly outside the opening but still mostly obscured by the arm and bag folds. The wooden worktable supports both objects. The computer tower and mounting frame remain unchanged, with electrical cables curving around the two differently elevated wrists.",
      "Frame 29: The left/rear gripper now holds the Labubu plush toy clear of the wooden worktable, gripping near its long ears or upper head. The gray-beige fuzzy body hangs below, with a pale round face, dark eyes, and small limbs visible; a metallic-looking loop dangles at its side. The toy is separated from the pink bag below by roughly a toy-body length in the image. The bag lies open and flattened with white printing upward. The right/foreground gripper is raised and open to the toy's right. The computer tower, black mounting frame, and electrical cable bundle remain behind the lifted arms.",
      "Frame 30: The left/rear arm lowers the Labubu plush onto the pink bag. The toy is upright or slightly tilted, with its pale face toward the camera and its lower body contacting the bag on the wooden tabletop; the gripper still holds near its ears. The right/foreground gripper remains open and raised at the upper right, well clear of both objects. The pink bag spreads beneath the toy, with its drawstring visible to the left. The computer tower and mounting frame stay stationary. Electrical cables bend along the lowered left arm and suspended right wrist.",
      "Frame 31: The Labubu plush has been released and lies horizontally on the flattened pink bag, with its fuzzy gray-beige back facing upward and its face largely hidden. The bag has shifted toward the lower-right area of the wooden worktable, and a cream drawstring loop extends toward the lower left. Both grippers are open and lifting away: the left/rear gripper is high above the objects, while the right/foreground gripper retreats toward the right edge. The computer tower and black mounting frame become less obstructed. The electrical cable bundle follows the arms upward and outward.",
      "Frame 32: The pink bag and Labubu plush remain stationary on the wooden worktable in the lower-right portion of the view. The toy lies sideways across the bag, with its fuzzy back uppermost, while the cream drawstring rests in a loop beside the bag's lower-left edge. The left/rear gripper hovers open above and behind them, and the right/foreground gripper is open farther to the right, partially cropped; neither touches the objects, and clear gaps of roughly one to several gripper lengths remain in projection. The computer tower's illuminated fan, bolted black mounting frame, and routed electrical cables remain visible in the background."
